{"title":"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Reworded_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Reworded Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768f4e11a324ee335c6a0689a310fdaa8c33c921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-500,500]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> for which the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d3e744e99f3d1df0c7fd8c3fb4fbb7a6b3c228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(kx)=2\\log(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly one real solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f4ba2c0d18383edb9d5f4aab842badae5fc0e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] Label f;  f.p=fontsize(5);  xaxis(-3,3,Ticks(f,1.0)); yaxis(-3,26,Ticks(f,1.0)); real f(real x){return (x+2)^2;} real g(real x){return x*-1;} real h(real x){return x*-2;} real i(real x){return x*-3;} real j(real x){return x*8;} draw(graph(f,-2,3),green); draw(graph(g,-2,2),red); draw(graph(h,-2,1),red); draw(graph(i,-2,1/3),red); draw(graph(j,-0.25,3),red); [/asy]\" width=\"148\" height=\"668\" />\n</p><p>Note the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d3e744e99f3d1df0c7fd8c3fb4fbb7a6b3c228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(kx)=2\\log(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> is valid for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607a8b92e76fa945dfccef02e6997220330d6c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/16006035a143f38a65feda3d7f00f342580cb7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Now, we simplify the given expression:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35fd716413834241758aa296390ebf9d009b6aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(kx)=2\\log(x+2)=\\log((x+2)^2) \\implies kx=(x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"458\" height=\"21\" />. The last equation is derived by taking away the outside logs from the previous equation. \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a846d9b4773d207409648ac230c627159f8ac33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> is always non-negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61956d2f89769fa07ff4f1cae31eaf8074f7d726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> must also be non-negative; therefore this takes care of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607a8b92e76fa945dfccef02e6997220330d6c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> condition as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958fa26776f39b396f55c320bb2ccebb91c962b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we graph both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a846d9b4773d207409648ac230c627159f8ac33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> (the green graph) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61956d2f89769fa07ff4f1cae31eaf8074f7d726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> (the red graph for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/0822af569c1fd3ea2dffe859f52aa6dd813d80ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=-1,k=-2,k=-3,k=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"239\" height=\"16\" />) for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/16006035a143f38a65feda3d7f00f342580cb7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. It is easy to see that all negative values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> make the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d3e744e99f3d1df0c7fd8c3fb4fbb7a6b3c228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(kx)=2\\log(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" /> have only one solution. \n</p><p>However, there is also one positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that makes the equation only have one solution, as shown by the steepest line in the diagram. We can show that the slope of this line is a positive integer by setting the discriminant of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c1585989b39d317328d0747742b61e6f4125bc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+2)^2=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77eb455e13266e46765af4d7b5506c4e3a6b314d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60cf158c51fb96c3eb20da34f33501a79fbc2446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq k \\leq 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd14499bebbf7855623388869c0910c4a004bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> will intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baae600d8168b5ca2dc1bd68ce9c0302bf4754fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" /> twice, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa63d60cc8aca48394ff27f4c44aea311a1fd226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd14499bebbf7855623388869c0910c4a004bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> will never intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baae600d8168b5ca2dc1bd68ce9c0302bf4754fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> negative solutions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive solution, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e44b7de8ba14e987cb94543781629818c089c22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use an algebraic approach. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d3e744e99f3d1df0c7fd8c3fb4fbb7a6b3c228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(kx)=2\\log(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80923b279079cb9fa3fc1cb6ce79f6f5bd6bd23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx = (x+2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" /> (the converse isn't necessarily true!), or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/19782ce855bfb2cb7ffebcc35f7a7a81f8a621e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+(4-k)x+4=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"19\" />. Our original equation has exactly one solution if and only if there is only one solution to the above equation, or one of the solutions is extraneous; it involves the computation of the log of a nonpositive number.\n</p><p>For the first case, this can only occur when it is a perfect square trinomial, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6460a1d6d771c6cdf2f734c66de93c30372d4ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84574de7797bc7b4e1fc52075f4d265ba60a8bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d515f3392ff7472c334c1750d74d2c417b586683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> on the left side, which is invalid. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/9807ed176ecfd75ce05044e410875fb94d525520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, so that is one solution.\n</p><p>For the second case, we can use the quadratic formula. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454d2ca4691e953c7b06166e76e064c69d1f01aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{k-4 \\pm \\sqrt{k^2-8k}}2,\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"40\" /> so for there to be at least one real solution, the discriminant must be nonnegative, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90947babbaa4c8f30c113d197f17b73a0c46f449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90947babbaa4c8f30c113d197f17b73a0c46f449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then both solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> will be positive, and therefore both valid, which means all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are unsatisfactory. \n</p><p>We now wish to show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then exactly one solution works. Note that whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, both \"solutions\" in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are negative. One of the solutions to the equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa44c84b736dc699ff00c22b48a0759553bcf33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{k-4 + \\sqrt{k^2-8k}}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"174\" height=\"40\" />. We wish to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/39440c2633426c2d196ef36832e23197add1d690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b344183277ce5de15c7858945112b3a28beef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> (therefore the RHS in the original equation will be defined). Substituting, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769ab4a426cfb44ee62ede2f6c1c918a391696b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k-4 + \\sqrt{k^2-8k}}2 &gt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"188\" height=\"40\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c6fc12eedadd3d7192fa2959de0224d49d972d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{k^2 - 8k} &gt; -k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. Since both sides are positive, we can square both sides (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c558f282fa4cb6df5aab4a7b9b962d4f7afd6b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-k &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />) to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af312fd1d9632756b7ad69213d113fce61841663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2-8k &gt; k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed8a2abb30025d1aeea66051ef9b2168ce83781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8k &lt; 0 \\implies k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />, which was our original assumption, so this solution satisfies the original equation. The other case is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e4458249a2952404b9db86614345f2e4df7717fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{k-4 - \\sqrt{k^2-8k}}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"174\" height=\"40\" />, which we wish to show is less that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e089b1b86871bfe68fc6f6fe9d6d3d9dd4159d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k-4 - \\sqrt{k^2-8k}}2 &lt; -2 \\implies k &lt; \\sqrt{k^2-8k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"347\" height=\"40\" />. However, since the square root is defined to be positive, then this is always true, which implies that whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, there is exactly one real solution that satisfies the original equation. Combining this with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299e95443bb1cebd50bd9af8bebddf923ccfd9cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in [-500, 500]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, we find that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d2e35d1cf852dc8d50cc3fcbf93ae0076ce63f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500 + 1 = \\boxed{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The key to this solution is understanding that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad84e53f841dc8fd6f960de743a529539e433ff1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> has a domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fcfe836b7cf0b8388c9ec65707808f5dadccd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2, \\infty),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> so in the second case, when there are two possible solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f3824cccea4a7bcc3037d799d684e67bca4c69ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> we notice that only the interval of the greater solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb3399f288c7a28ac2484b7bba72654ee4d9772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> works, which means that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b043119262a2beb49176cb4beb5c50ec1915a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> will have exactly one solution.\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Reworded_Solution_2\">Reworded Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Reworded Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Immediately we notice if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is non-zero we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8dceb9c2b584d1a6e2f07bbd5fe29f68594aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx, (x+2) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> for our sole solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1675adffd995bc1a55cdae33f5170e0d59e23f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />. Simplifying the logarithmic equation we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fc3199362222b0a2b8fe3c577c4a5e7e5bad4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx = (x+2)^2 \\rightarrow 0 = x^2 + (4-k)x + 4 \\rightarrow x = \\frac{k-4 \\pm \\sqrt{k^2 - 8k}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"513\" height=\"43\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9f6bb5e759a18d6917e0568f6fb0c647404492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa5708af0f0203c0449fd3b072c470f66abef68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/9807ed176ecfd75ce05044e410875fb94d525520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> we have exactly one real solution (easily verifiable). Notice when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90947babbaa4c8f30c113d197f17b73a0c46f449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, both solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are positive, and so all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is not satisfactory. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b634700c95ed9caa5d7bf32c919a89a97dc9a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> it can be shown that the greater solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb3399f288c7a28ac2484b7bba72654ee4d9772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and the lesser solution is in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb688c186303493e51f4c1391220d39840994367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2,-\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> which is satisfactory. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037759bd1c0d643d061ef318755dded992bd956e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 8,-1,-2,...,-500 \\rightarrow \\boxed{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"247\" height=\"25\" /> satisfactory integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~FRIDAY\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II\" title=\"2017 AIME II\">2017 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external te